{"id":"mahabharata-3-156","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":156,"title":"षट्पञ्चाशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 156 · Arshtishena's counsel","summary":{"en":"The aged ascetic Arshtishena welcomes them and describes the wonders of the mountain, where gods and Kinnaras sport on the peaks. He warns them not to go further but to stay there calmly until Arjuna comes.","kn":"ವೃದ್ಧ ತಪಸ್ವಿ ಆರ್ಷ್ಟಿಷೇಣನು ಅವರನ್ನು ಸ್ವಾಗತಿಸಿ, ಶಿಖರಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ದೇವತೆಗಳು ಕಿನ್ನರರು ವಿಹರಿಸುವ ಪರ್ವತದ ಅದ್ಭುತಗಳನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಮುಂದೆ ಹೋಗದೆ ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಬರುವವರೆಗೆ ಶಾಂತವಾಗಿ ಇಲ್ಲೇ ಇರಿ ಎಂದು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"वृद्ध तपस्वी आर्ष्टिषेण उनका स्वागत करते हैं और उस पर्वत के आश्चर्यों का वर्णन करते हैं, जहाँ शिखरों पर देवता और किन्नर विहार करते हैं। वे चेतावनी देते हैं कि आगे न जाएँ, बल्कि अर्जुन के आने तक शान्ति से वहीं रहें।","te":"వృద్ధ తాపసి ఆర్ష్టిషేణుడు వారిని స్వాగతించి, శిఖరాలపై దేవతలు, కిన్నరులు విహరించే పర్వతపు అద్భుతాలను వర్ణిస్తాడు. ముందుకు వెళ్లకుండా అర్జునుడు వచ్చే వరకు ప్రశాంతంగా ఇక్కడే ఉండమని హెచ్చరిస్తాడు.","ta":"முதிய தவசி ஆர்ஷ்டிஷேணர் அவர்களை வரவேற்று, சிகரங்களில் தேவர்களும் கின்னரர்களும் விளையாடும் மலையின் அதிசயங்களை வர்ணிக்கிறார். மேலே செல்லாமல் அர்ஜுனன் வரும் வரை அமைதியாக இங்கேயே தங்குமாறு எச்சரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"വൃദ്ധനായ തപസ്വി അർഷ്ടിഷേണൻ അവരെ സ്വാഗതം ചെയ്ത്, ദേവന്മാരും കിന്നരന്മാരും കൊടുമുടികളിൽ വിഹരിക്കുന്ന പർവതത്തിന്റെ അത്ഭുതങ്ങൾ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. ഇനി മുന്നോട്ട് പോകരുതെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു; അർജുനൻ വരുംവരെ അവിടെ ശാന്തമായി താമസിക്കണമെന്ന് ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.156; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"यक्षयुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Yakshayuddha Parva (Battle with the Yakshas)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्तमासाद्य तपसा दग्धकिल्बिषम् ।\nअभ्यवादयत प्रीतः शिरसा नाम कीर्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira approached him, whose sins were burned away by austerity, and gladly greeted him, bowing his head and speaking his name."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततः कृष्णा च भीमश्च यमौ चापि यशस्विनौ ।\nशिरोभिः प्राप्य राजर्षिं परिवार्योपतस्थिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Krishna Draupadi, Bhima and the two renowned twins also bowed their heads to the royal sage and stood around him."}},{"n":3,"text":"तथैव धौम्यो धर्मज्ञः पाण्डवानां पुरोहितः ।\nयथान्यायमुपाक्रान्तस्तमृषिं संशितव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise Dhaumya, the Pandavas' priest and knower of dharma, duly approached that sage of firm vows."}},{"n":4,"text":"अन्वजानात्स धर्मज्ञो मुनिर्दिव्येन चक्षुषा ।\nपाण्डोः पुत्रान्कुरुश्रेष्ठानास्यतामिति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage, knower of dharma, with divine sight, welcomed the sons of Pandu, best of the Kurus, and told them to sit."}},{"n":5,"text":"कुरूणामृषभं प्राज्ञं पूजयित्वा महातपाः ।\nसह भ्रातृभिरासीनं पर्यपृच्छदनामयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great ascetic honoured the wise bull of the Kurus, and when he was seated with his brothers, asked after his welfare."}},{"n":6,"text":"नानृते कुरुषे भावं कच्चिद्धर्मे च वर्तसे ।\nमतापित्रोश्च ते वृत्तिः कच्चित्पार्थ न सीदति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Does your mind not lean to falsehood, and do you keep to dharma? Son of Pritha, does your care for your mother and father not fail?\""}},{"n":7,"text":"कच्चित्ते गुरवः सर्वे वृद्धा वैद्याश्च पूजिताः ।\nकच्चिन्न कुरुषे भावं पार्थ पापेषु कर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Are all your teachers, elders and physicians honoured? Do you not let your mind dwell on evil deeds, Partha?\""}},{"n":8,"text":"सुकृतं प्रतिकर्तुं च कच्चिद्धातुं च दुष्कृतम् ।\nयथान्यायं कुरुश्रेष्ठ जानासि न च कत्थसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of the Kurus, do you know how to repay a kindness and to put down a wrong in the proper way, without boasting?\""}},{"n":9,"text":"यथार्हं मानिताः कच्चित्त्वया नन्दन्ति साधवः ।\nवनेष्वपि वसन्कच्चिद्धर्ममेवानुवर्तसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Do the good rejoice at being honoured by you as they deserve? Even living in the forest, do you follow dharma alone?\""}},{"n":10,"text":"कच्चिद्धौम्यस्त्वदाचारैर्न पार्थ परितप्यते ।\nदानधर्मतपःशौचैरार्जवेन तितिक्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Does Dhaumya not suffer distress, Partha, over your conduct, as to giving, dharma, austerity, purity, honesty and patience?\""}},{"n":11,"text":"पितृपैतामहं वृत्तं कच्चित्पार्थानुवर्तसे ।\nकच्चिद्राजर्षियातेन पथा गच्छसि पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Son of Pritha, do you follow the conduct of your father and grandfather? Do you walk, Pandava, in the path travelled by royal sages?\""}},{"n":12,"text":"स्वे स्वे किल कुले जाते पुत्रे नप्तरि वा पुनः ।\nपितरः पितृलोकस्थाः शोचन्ति च हसन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For when a son or grandson is born in each family, the ancestors who dwell in the world of the fathers grieve and also laugh.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"किं न्वस्य दुष्कृतेऽस्माभिः संप्राप्तव्यं भविष्यति ।\nकिं चास्य सुकृतेऽस्माभिः प्राप्तव्यमिति शोभनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They wonder: 'What will we get for his evil deed? And what good will we obtain for his good deed?'\""}},{"n":14,"text":"पिता माता तथैवाग्निर्गुरुरात्मा च पञ्चमः ।\nयस्यैते पूजिताः पार्थ तस्य लोकावुभौ जितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Father, mother, fire, teacher, and the self as the fifth: whoever honours these, Partha, has won both worlds.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"अब्भक्षा वायुभक्षाश्च प्लवमाना विहायसा ।\nजुषन्ते पर्वतश्रेष्ठमृषयः पर्वसंधिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sages, living on water and air, float through the sky and visit the best of mountains at the junctions of the lunar phases.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"कामिनः सह कान्ताभिः परस्परमनुव्रताः ।\nदृश्यन्ते शैलशृङ्गस्थास्तथा किंपुरुषा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kimpurushas, king, are seen standing on the mountain peaks with their beloved women, devoted to one another and full of love.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"अरजांसि च वासांसि वसानाः कौशिकानि च ।\nदृश्यन्ते बहवः पार्थ गन्धर्वाप्सरसां गणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Many troops of Gandharvas and Apsarases, wearing spotless silk garments, are seen, Partha.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"विद्याधरगणाश्चैव स्रग्विणः प्रियदर्शनाः ।\nमहोरगगणाश्चैव सुपर्णाश्चोरगादयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Troops of Vidyadharas, garlanded and pleasant to see, and troops of great serpents, Suparnas and snakes, are also seen.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"अस्य चोपरि शैलस्य श्रूयते पर्वसंधिषु ।\nभेरीपणवशङ्खानां मृदङ्गानां च निस्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"On top of this mountain, at the junctions of the lunar phases, the sound of kettledrums, tabors, conches and mridangas is heard.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"इहस्थैरेव तत्सर्वं श्रोतव्यं भरतर्षभाः ।\nन कार्या वः कथंचित्स्यात्तत्राभिसरणे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All that must be heard from where you are, bulls of the Bharatas. You must not in any way set your mind on going there.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"न चाप्यतः परं शक्यं गन्तुं भरतसत्तमाः ।\nविहारो ह्यत्र देवानाममानुषगतिस्तु सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Nor, best of the Bharatas, can anyone go beyond this point. This is the playground of the gods, and the way there is not for humans.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"ईषच्चपलकर्माणं मनुष्यमिह भारत ।\nद्विषन्ति सर्वभूतानि ताडयन्ति च राक्षसाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bharata, all creatures hate a man here of even slightly fickle behaviour, and rakshasas strike him.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"अभ्यतिक्रम्य शिखरं शैलस्यास्य युधिष्ठिर ।\nगतिः परमसिद्धानां देवर्षीणां प्रकाशते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Beyond the summit of this mountain, Yudhishthira, the path of the greatest Siddhas and divine sages opens.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"चापलादिह गच्छन्तं पार्थ यानमतः परम् ।\nअयःशूलादिभिर्घ्नन्ति राक्षसाः शत्रुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Anyone who goes on beyond this from rashness, Partha, scourge of foes, is struck by rakshasas with iron spears and other weapons.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"अप्सरोभिः परिवृतः समृद्ध्या नरवाहनः ।\nइह वैश्रवणस्तात पर्वसंधिषु दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Here, dear one, at the junctions of the lunar phases, Vaishravana is seen, surrounded by Apsarases, with great wealth, carried by men.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"शिखरे तं समासीनमधिपं सर्वरक्षसाम् ।\nप्रेक्षन्ते सर्वभूतानि भानुमन्तमिवोदितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All creatures see him, the lord of all rakshasas, seated on the peak like the risen sun.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"देवदानवसिद्धानां तथा वैश्रवणस्य च ।\nगिरेः शिखरमुद्यानमिदं भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This mountain peak, best of the Bharatas, is the pleasure garden of gods, danavas, Siddhas and Vaishravana.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"उपासीनस्य धनदं तुम्बुरोः पर्वसंधिषु ।\nगीतसामस्वनस्तात श्रूयते गन्धमादने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"At the junctions of the lunar phases, dear one, the sound of Tumburu singing the Sama chants, attending the giver of wealth, is heard on Gandhamadana.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"एतदेवंविधं चित्रमिह तात युधिष्ठिर ।\nप्रेक्षन्ते सर्वभूतानि बहुशः पर्वसंधिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This kind of wonder, dear Yudhishthira, is seen by all creatures here many times at the junctions of the lunar phases.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"भुञ्जानाः सर्वभोज्यानि रसवन्ति फलानि च ।\nवसध्वं पाण्डवश्रेष्ठा यावदर्जुनदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Eat all the foods and juicy fruits, and stay, best of the Pandavas, until you see Arjuna.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"न तात चपलैर्भाव्यमिह प्राप्तैः कथंचन ।\nउषित्वेह यथाकामं यथाश्रद्धं विहृत्य च ।\nततः शस्त्रभृतां श्रेष्ठ पृथिवीं पालयिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dear one, do not be fickle in any way now you have come here. When you have lived here as you wish and played as you like, then, best of weapon-bearers, you will rule the earth.\""}}]}]}